**Figure 1.2.2 – Detailed Electrical Schematic of the Automatic Ice Cream Dispensing Module**

Figure 1.2.2 presents the detailed electrical schematic of the automatic ice cream dispensing control circuit, including the STM32 Blue Pill, TTL-to-RS485 Converter Module (MAX485), two PC817 optocouplers, BTS7960 Motor Driver Module, LM2596 Step-Down Voltage Regulator, two KW12-071 limit switches, and 330 Ω and 4.7 kΩ resistors. Matching signal labels identify electrically connected points.

STM32 PA9 and PA10 connect to MAX485 DI and RO, respectively; PA4 connects to both DE and /RE to select transmission or reception. PA8 and PB1 connect to pin 1 of the two PC817 optocouplers, with each pin 2 connected through a 330 Ω resistor to GND_ADAPTER. On the output side, each PC817 pin 4 connects to the LM2596-derived 5 V supply. Pin 3 connects to BTS7960 RPWM or LPWM, respectively, and through a 4.7 kΩ pull-down resistor to OUT−. BTS7960 VCC, L_EN, and R_EN connect to this 5 V supply.

PB0 is labeled UPPER_LIMIT and PB10 is labeled LOWER_LIMIT. Each signal connects through a 4.7 kΩ series resistor to the corresponding switch COM terminal; NO connects to GND_ADAPTER and NC is left open. Both inputs use the STM32 internal pull-up resistors to provide active-low limit signals. The switch series resistors serve a different role from the pull-down resistors on the PC817 outputs.

The +5V_ADAPTER and GND_ADAPTER supply the STM32/MAX485 side and provide the reference for both switches. The +24V rail supplies BTS7960 B+ and LM2596 IN+, while B− and IN− connect to the power-side GND. LM2596 OUT+ provides the 5 V rail for the BTS7960/PC817 side, and OUT− connects to BTS7960 logic GND. The supply labels distinguish the control and power domains.

External connections are not repeated in Figure 1.2.2: MAX485 A/B connect to the USB-to-RS485 Converter, and BTS7960 M+/M− connect to the JGB37-520 motor, as shown in Figure 1.2.1. The 5 V adapter and 24 V supply are represented by their respective supply labels.

